    <bpmn:task id="Bridge_2_d312" name="Here are two options for a concise transition sentence:&#10;&#10;**Option 1 (Focus on the deployed solution):**&#10;&#62; If the deployed IT solution is a smartphone, and its screen subsequently breaks, the employee may then use the DIY repair tool to fix it.&#10;&#10;**Option 2 (Focus on the employee action):**&#10;&#62; If an employee damages their smartphone (a potential solution deployed in Process A), this incident could prompt them to utilize the DIY repair tool described in Process B.&#10;&#10;**Why these work:**&#10;*   They logically connect the outcome of A (a deployed smartphone solution being in use) to the trigger for B (that smartphone breaking).&#10;*   They are concise (each is one sentence).&#10;*   They explicitly state that the damage to the *deployed solution* is what initiates Process B." />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2B_2" sourceRef="atom_1_ExclusiveGateway_5" targetRef="Bridge_2_d312" />
